session:pr664Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #500 asked for the ObjectProperty: frame's SubPropertyChain: section (object property chains), the fourth of six grammar productions split out of umbrella issue #157, using #499 (HasKey:) as the closest template in the same crate. Unlike HasKey:'s property list, SubPropertyChain: has no ambiguity to resolve: every chain item is unconditionally an objectPropertyExpression (data properties don't participate in property chains at all), so no analogue of #499's pre-scanned is_known_data_property disambiguation table was needed -- property_expression_chain reuses property_expr::object_property_expression directly. The one deliberate departure from the obvious separated_list1(keyword(\"o\"), ...) implementation: that combinator alone would also accept a single element with no 'o' at all, silently misparsing what the W3C grammar (objectPropertyExpression 'o' objectPropertyExpression { 'o' objectPropertyExpression }) requires to be an error. The parser instead parses one element then requires many1(preceded(keyword(\"o\"), ...)), enforcing the >=2 arity by construction; a negative test (SubPropertyChain: hasParent, no 'o') was added to pin this down after an advisor review caught that the initial separated_list1 draft would have silently accepted it. A second decision, structurally different from every other ObjectProperty: frame section: for SubPropertyChain:, the frame's own property is the axiom's super-property and the section's value is the sub-side (the chain) -- the reverse of SubPropertyOf:'s roles. This maps directly onto the pre-existing owl_ontology::SubPropertyExpression::PropertyExpressionChain variant with no new axiom type needed. Before implementing, grepped owl2rl2datalog/eli/rdf_owl_translator for PropertyExpressionChain/ObjectPropertyChain and confirmed downstream translation (owl2rl2datalog's prp-spo2 rule) already exists and needed no changes -- this issue was pure parser/serializer surface, not a reasoning-side gap. serialize.rs frames the chain under the super-property, joining formatted elements with \" o \", following the same skip-on-non-representable-shape discipline (log_skip, never invalid syntax) as every other serializer arm. Separately, this PR's CI is red for a reason unrelated to the change itself: origin/main was found broken at the merge-base commit (dagalog-kernel's dispatch_cell missing a .map_err on its Functional arm) -- already filed as #662 by another agent before this session checked, so no duplicate issue was filed; the PR body documents the dependency on #662 landing first." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:664 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr664 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .
